                            <h1 class="blog-heading-css">Digital Marketing Salary in India</h1>
                            <a href="#"><img src="img/Digital Marketing Salary in India.webp" class="img-responsive" alt="Digital Marketing salary in India 2022" /></a><br>
                            <div class="cus-bullet">
                                <h3>TABLE OF CONTENT</h3>
                                <li><a href="#1">Search Engine Optimization Expert Salary</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#2">Expert in Pay-Per-Click (PPC)</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#3">Web Developer</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#4">Social media marketing expert</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#5">Data Analyst</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#6">Expert in Paid Media</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#7">Digital Marketing Manager</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#8">Marketing Automation Professional</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#9">Content Marketing Manager</a></li>
                              	
                              		
                            </div>
                            
                          
                            <p class="span">
                                The rise of digital marketing over traditional marketing has benefited businesses while also providing chances for digital marketers to enhance their careers. Because this is such a large business, the salary growth prospects for Digital Marketing have changed throughout time and continue to be very dynamic for the better. However, the initial salary for a digital marketer is minimal, and it increases as you get experience and upskill.<br><br>
                                The following are <b>digital marketing salaries in 2024</b>  for various digital marketing job roles:
                                


                                </p>

                            
                            
                                <h4 class="text-transf" id="1">Search Engine Optimization Expert Salary</h3>
                                <p class="span">
                                    The main goal of a <a href="https://www.kingofdigitalmarketing.com/SEO-Services.aspx"> Search Engine Optimization</a> Specialist is to produce targeted website traffic and have it rank on the top page of Google for relevant keywords.<br><br>
                                    An entry-level <b>digital marketing salary in India</b>  is 1,76,578 per year for a SEO Specialist with less than one year of experience. A SEO Specialist with fewer than four years of experience can expect to earn an average of 234,460 rupees in India. SEO Specialists with 5 to 9 years of experience can expect to earn an average of 4,58,532 rupees in India.
                                    

                                  </p>
                        
                            
                                   

                                  <a href="#"><img src="images/busines-venture.webp" class="img-responsive" alt="google-trends" /></a><br>


                            <h4 class="text-transf" id="2">Expert in Pay-Per-Click (PPC)</h4>
                            <p class="span">
                                <a href="	
                                https://www.kingofdigitalmarketing.com/blog/best-ppc-services-in-delhi.html"> PPC Executives</a> are in charge of administering Paid Ad Campaigns on Google Ads and other Ad Networks.<br><br>
                              An entry-level PPC Expert in India with less than a year of experience makes around 3 lakhs per year. A PPC Expert with more than two years of experience in India may expect to earn roughly 4-5 lakhs per year in India.


                               </p>

                              
                            
                            
                                    
                            <h4 class="text-transf" id="3">Web Developer</h4>
                            <p class="span">
                                In the sector of <a href="https://www.kingofdigitalmarketing.com/Website-Development.aspx
                                "> Website Design </a> the <b>digital marketing salary</b> is also very high. A web developer should be knowledgeable about the many coding languages in use and have the ability to design a functional and appealing website for the company.<br><br>
                                In India, a Web designer with less than one year of experience can expect to earn 2 lakhs per year as an entry-level digital marketing pay, while those with more than 2-3 years of experience can expect to earn 3-5 lakhs per year.
                                
                            </p>


                            <a href="#"><img src="images/webdeveloper.webp" class="img-responsive" alt="webdeveloper" /></a><br>
                                

                            <h4 class="text-transf" id="4">Social media marketing expert</h4>
                            <p class="span">
                                If you enjoy using social media to create money, now is the time to do it. Social Media Marketing experts plan and execute a company's whole social media strategy.<br><br>
                                An entry-level <b>digital marketing salary in India</b> for a Social Media Marketing Specialist with less than a year of experience is 2,52,444 INR.
                                People with 5 to 9 years ' experience to earn an average of 6,85,923 per year in India.
                                
                                
                                </p>
                               
                              

                            

                                    <h4 class="text-transf" id="5">Data Analyst</h4>
                                <p class="span">
                                    A Data Analyst analyses data and transforms it into information that can be used to improve business choices.
                                    The average entry-level <b>digital marketing salary in India</b> is 3 lakhs; however, a data analyst with more than 2-3 years of experience might make a yearly income of 4-5 lakhs.
                                    </p>


                                   
                                    

                                    <h4 class="text-transf" id="6">Expert in Paid Media</h4>
                                    <p class="span">
                                        A paid media specialist is in charge of increasing traffic to your website through online advertising on platforms like Facebook, Instagram, and Google.<br><br>
                                        An entry-level Paid Media professional can earn a <b>digital marketing salary</b> of 3 lakhs per year at first, but as your experience and competence improve, your income will rise. A paid media specialist with more than 2-3 years of experience in India may expect to earn roughly 5-6 lakhs per year in India.
                                        
                                        </p>

                                        <a href="#"><img src="images/job-security.webp" class="img-responsive" alt="google-trends" /></a><br>

                                        <h4 class="text-transf" id="7">Digital Marketing Manager</h4>
                                    <p class="span">
                                        The entire online presence of a firm is planned and implemented by digital marketing managers.<br><br>
                                        A Digital Marketing Manager (entry-level) in  earns an average of 5,48,755 rupees per year in India. The senior digital marketing managers make between Rs 7,09,800 and Rs 10,00,000.
                                         </p>
 
                                        <h4 class="text-transf" id="8">Marketing Automation Professional</h4>
                                    <p class="span">
                                        A Marketing Automation expert is in charge of maintaining and improving the capabilities of the marketing automation platform.
                                        In India, an entry-level Marketing Automation Manager with less than a year of experience earns Rs. 4 lakhs a year.<br><br>
                                        A Marketing Automation Manager with at least 2-3 years of experience can expect to make roughly Rs. 6 lakh per year.
                                       
                                        </p>

                                        <h4 class="text-transf" id="9">Content Marketing Manager</h4>
                                        <p class="span">
                                           <a href=" https://www.kingofdigitalmarketing.com/Content-Writing-Service.aspx ">Content marketing</a> managers are in charge of an organization's overall content strategy and creation among all platforms.
                                            An entry-level <b>digital marketing salary in India</b> for a Content Marketing Manager is expected to be roughly 4,79,323. A Content Marketing Manager with less than 4 years of experience in India can expect to earn on average 5,13,369 rupees.<br><br>
                                            
                                            To conclude, the potential of digital marketers is here to stay and will only increase in the coming years. Due to its dynamic nature and enormous learning opportunities, it is certain to become a dream career path for the youth.
                                            Keep in mind, however, that your revenue as a digital marketer will be totally defined by your experience and how well you upskill to keep up with current trends.
                                            
                                            
    
                                            
                                            </p>                   

